    "nuance_en": "'ために' represents: <strong>in order to; for the purpose of; because of</strong>. It is an essential JLPT N3 intermediate pattern used to express specific speaker stances, modal judgments, and emotional colorings with natural fluency.",
    "trap_ja": "<ruby>英語<rt>えいご</rt></ruby>の<ruby>語義<rt>ごぎ</rt></ruby> <strong>\"in order to; for the purpose of; because of\"</strong> を<ruby>表層<rt>ひょうそう</rt></ruby><ruby>的<rt>てき</rt></ruby>に<ruby>直訳<rt>ちょくやく</rt></ruby>してそのまま<ruby>日本語<rt>にほんご</rt></ruby>に<ruby>当<rt>あ</rt></ruby>てはめると、<ruby>文脈<rt>ぶんみゃく</rt></ruby>の<ruby>敬意<rt>けいい</rt></ruby>や<ruby>制限<rt>せいげん</rt></ruby>（ポジティブ／ネガティブ<ruby>限定<rt>げんてい</rt></ruby>、<ruby>目上<rt>めうえ</rt></ruby>の<ruby>人<rt>ひと</rt></ruby>への<ruby>使用<rt>しよう</rt></ruby><ruby>可否<rt>かひ</rt></ruby>など）を<ruby>無視<rt>むし</rt></ruby>した<ruby>不自然<rt>ふしぜん</rt></ruby>な<ruby>文<rt>ぶん</rt></ruby>になりがちです。<ruby>助詞<rt>じょし</rt></ruby>の<ruby>選択<rt>せんたく</rt></ruby>や<ruby>前後<rt>ぜんご</rt></ruby>の<ruby>修飾<rt>しゅうしょく</rt></ruby><ruby>関係<rt>かんけい</rt></ruby>を<ruby>必<rt>かなら</rt></ruby>ず<ruby>確認<rt>かくにん</rt></ruby>しましょう。",
    "trap_en": "Literal translation of \"in order to; for the purpose of; because of\" without considering Japanese grammatical constraints frequently leads to awkward phrasing. Be mindful of polarity (positive vs negative constraints) and formal register.",
